{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1451731-ideas-for-making-the-briarnet-distinct","id":1451731,"title":"Ideas for making the BriarNet distinct","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-06-11T13:29:17-07:00","id":1451731,"title":"Ideas for making the BriarNet distinct","content":"Hey I have a player who wants to explore the BriarNet which seems to both be the hedge internet and a location/realm in the hedge at the same time. So I wanted some ideas from people who know more so I know how to best portray and use the BriarNet in my game....so input peepz?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-12T00:12:43-07:00","id":1451807,"title":"","content":"<br /> &quot;<i>Face-to-face gatherings occur in shared Hollows they call the Clouds: literal cloud-chambers, each keyed to a secret web address, floating in the sky of the BriarNet - the digital Hedge.&quot; </i> <div align=\"right\">pg. 23; <i>Oak, Ash, &amp; Thorn: The Changeling: The Lost Second Edition Companion </i><br /> <br /> </div> The BriarNet is introduced in tandem with the example Free Company, The Crystal Webb (a non-traditional mantle group). Their Common and Royal contracts extend the effects of the BriarNet from the Hedge into the mundane world (allowing hedgespinning within electronics for example). However, the BriarNet itself isn't concretely outlined.<ul><li>Clouds (BriarNet Hollows) are keyed to secret web addresses <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">(above quote) </span></li> <li>&quot;<i>The changeling becomes one of countless nodes along the BriarNet's information superhighway</i>&quot; <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">(Contract: Hidden Protocal (Common))</span></li> <li>&quot;...<i>may watch the information pass by inside the BriarNet (whether as a news crawl on a private channel or a biplane trailing a banner across a hidden sky)</i>&quot;.<span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><i>(Contract: Hidden Protocol (Common))</i></span></li> <li>&quot;the changeling stands on the trod within the BriarNet and opens a digital Hedgeway&quot; <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">(<i>Contract: Autonomous Payload (Royal))</i></span></li> <li><i>&quot;While the contract is active, the changeling may navigate to a BriarNet representation of a signal or network (if the repository is thus connected)&quot; <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">((Contract: Autonomous Payload (Royal))</span></i></li> </ul>From the above, we know the BriarNet: has Hollows; it functions along nodes (which The Crystal Webb members can count themselves as one via their Common contract); has trods; can have digital Hedgeways opened (via The Crystal Webb's Royal Contract); exists as a space where private channels and biplanes coexist. <br /> <br /> As a note, I can't find a single example where a non-Crystal Webb member interacts with the BriarNet. It's not to state it precludes someone from doing so, but that's an ST call. A lot of interactions with the BriarNet are barred by this Free Company's exclusive contracts. If your player is looking for immediate affiliation, I would suggest they be/become a member. <br /> <br /> <b>ST Creative-Fodder: </b><br /> 1. How do player's not affiliated with The Crystal Webb gain access to the BriarNet? <br /> 2. With Clouds being keyed to Secret web addresses - do you have to be in the Hedge to input said key (and if so, where) or does access via URL input in the mundane transport one to the Hollow? <br /> 3. What is the BriarNet's relationship spatially to the Hedge? Is it a &quot;hidden level&quot;? <br /> <br /> <b>DriveThruRPG Link: Oak, Ash, &amp; Thorn (PDF; 6.99 USD)</b><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/306076/Oak-Ash-and-Thorn-The-Changeling-The-Lost-Second-Edition-Companion\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/images/4261/306076.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/306076/Oak-Ash-and-Thorn-The-Changeling-The-Lost-Second-Edition-Companion\" target=\"_blank\"> Oak, Ash, and Thorn: The Changeling: The Lost Second Edition Companion - Onyx Path Publishing | Changeling: The Lost | DriveThruRPG.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/306076/Oak-Ash-and-Thorn-The-Changeling-The-Lost-Second-Edition-Companion\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/306076/Oak-Ash-and-Thorn-The-Changeling-The-Lost-Second-Edition-Companion </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Oak, Ash, and Thorn: The Changeling: The Lost Second Edition Companion - So, you&rsquo;re home. What now?Gonna run and hide for the rest of your life to make sure They never find you again? Screw t </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14918-ashes","name":"Ashes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-21T15:59:54-07:00","id":1453088,"title":"","content":"This is my two cents and headcanon.<br /> <br /> BriarNet is an evolution of the Hedge, born from humanity's collective shift in subconcious recognition of danger and mystery. A modern kid is much more likely to 'get lost' playing a video game or falling down a youtube rabbit hole than running wild through the neighborhood and finding the 'creepy' witch house on the corner with their friends. How many parents have threatened kids that the tv or video games would 'rot their brain' if they watch it too much, and now it actually happens with rotting fetches made of mouldering leaves and fruit taking their place when the parents are tucked away in their home office and the kid is unsupervised for hours? <br /> <br /> I wouldn't think that the BriarNet is Crystal Web exclusive, but it might be more rare for other changelings to really figure it out. Like the internet that is 'everywhere', the BriarNet is 'everywhere' in the Hedge. It connects nodes wirelessly through the 'cloud' (which may have poor reception on a bright and sunny day in the Hedge, and better reception when overcast or raining. heheh) but cut away at a patch of brambles out in the Hedge and you might find a 'fiber' line running through the brambles. Maybe a freehold has tapped into one of these lines in the thorns to provide BriarNet access for its members. Maybe an Autumn has hooked a line up to an old fashioned loud speaker to provide wireless access. <br /> <br /> Like the internet, some sites/nodes are private and need a password to access, and others are public and can be accessed from anywhere. There's a massive goblin market in the BriarNet with everything you could ever think of on offer, that can easily be accessed from anywhere if you have BriarNet access... but there's a dark side to it. Your local goblin market has been raided regularly, vendors blackmailed into moving their goods to the BriarNet. Prices are being driven down, and the downsides of goblin contracts are getting worse. Changelings around the world drowning in goblin debt and are starting to be forced to work for the market in terrible Arcadian-esque conditions in order to pay it off...<br /> <br /> Overall, the Hedge and BriarNet may generally appear and function similarly but what you can get there is different. The regular Hedge has goblin fruit and other (often) physical challenges to face. The Dreaming Roads connect the Hedge to the dreams and psychic phenomena. The BriarNet stretches this border area into an Intellectual realm and fundamentally provides access to data (academic and occult knowledge, political intelligence, social blackmail, etc) and the challenges that might surround it. Are there other lesser-known and used paths that intersect the Hedge? Probably! Or if there isn't yet, there certainly will be in the future when humanity dreams up something new. It seems like an excellent topic of study for an Autumn to take up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}